final fantasy 15 is right around the  corner and I basically know nothing  about it or any of the Final Fantasy  games for that matter in fact the only  Final Fantasy games I've played are 3 7  10 13 and crystal chronicles that may  sound like a decent amount but I didn't  finish any of them and 13 left a pretty  bad taste in my mouth  worst birthday ever for lack of a better  term I'm a Final Fantasy scrub but  considering I was 13 when Final Fantasy  15 or vs. at the time was announced I'm  kind of curious to see how this game  turned out so when we got access to a  final preview bill to the game I decided  to give it a shot and hopefully answer a  question that some of you might have is  it too late to play a Final Fantasy game  Final Fantasy 15 has new characters and  a new story but it's also the 15th main  line game in a series that has been  around for 30 years  [Music]  whether or not you've played Final  Fantasy there's no denying how  breathtaking this game is the vistas are  jaw-dropping the animations look  authentic and the scale is really  impressive not only is the map huge but  stumbling upon massive creatures are  huge monoliths scattered throughout the  world will leave you in awe even if you  don't know exactly what you're looking  at then the art direction certainly adds  to the visuals as well even though the  game is a fantasy game it manages to  avoid a lot of the genres tropes by  blending sci-fi tech with modern  inventions and classic fantasy elements  the Final Fantasy games have been doing  this for a while now but there's  something oddly compelling about taking  a road trip in a fantasy universe that  is strangely similar to our own at times  however the massive scale does come at a  cost I've only played around five hours  and I've spent a good amount of that  time behind the wheel on a chocobo or  just running  [Music]  if presentation and graphics aren't  really a selling point for you you might  have a difficult time getting into this  game but even if you do like visuals you  can only look at a virtual sunset and  sunrise so many times so the question is  how does this game play Final Fantasy's  combat has undergone many changes and  this one is very action-oriented if  you're expecting a turn-based JRPG with  an overworld and random encounters then  you might be happy to know that 15 does  none of these things creatures you fight  and have it the same space as you and  even though areas are sectioned off when  you begin a battle the transitions in  and out of combat are seamless once  you're in combat you'll be doing fairly  typical things like attacking blocking  parrying dodging countering and even  sneaking although it seems kind of out  of place in this game though the combat  itself is hard to compare to another  game it should feel familiar to those  who played action role-playing games  there are also things like link strikes  cooperative moves special abilities and  even spells that you can customize  although all these things are a little  convoluted a lot of these special moves  I flat-out ignored and I never really  felt like the game challenged me enough  to figure them out  as of many RPGs as you progress and  level up you will be able to unlock new  perks and skills for Noctis and his team  now I'm no stranger to unlock trees and  skill webs but Final Fantasy 15s  ascension system is a little bit  overwhelming fans of the series will  probably feel at home with something  like this but I had to spend a good  amount of time figuring out what  everything meant and what I should focus  on and what I should ignore now this  shouldn't come as a surprise but the  hardest thing for me to grasp in Final  Fantasy 15 is the story it isn't  necessarily hard to follow  it's just weird one moment I'm pushing a  car through a desert then I'm picking up  bounties at a roadside diner and then  I'm camping in a coma in tent cooking  eggs all while wearing black leather in  the desert although I kind of like the  quirkiness and attention to small  details that don't really matter but at  the same time isn't there a throne I'm  supposed to be taking because I don't  really think thumbing through pictures  is gonna help  and after 14 mainline games and dozens  of spin-offs Final Fantasy 15 has a  pretty well-established lore behind it a  lore that couldn't be more foreign to me  and I'm not even talking about the movie  and anime based around these characters  speaking of the characters five hours in  and I don't really like any of them they  don't even really seem like friends to  me just members in your party but like I  said I'm only five hours in in a game  that's supposed to be very very long so  hopefully that changes  there's a lot I don't understand about  Final Fantasy 15 and I'm sure some of it  will never make sense to me but after  the time I spent with the preview build  I really want to play more  I'm sure fans of the series will find  things that they love and things that  they hate but as someone who's never  particularly been invested in this  series now seems like a pretty good time  for me to start playing Final Fantasy  for more on Final Fantasy 15 in all  things gaming  stay tuned to game spot
 

